<title>ITALY: Italy says no aid for Olivetti outside EU rules.</title>
<headline>Italy says no aid for Olivetti outside EU rules.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industry minister Pierluigi Bersani said on Friday Italy had no intention of taking any measures to help troubled hi-tech group Olivetti which might infringe European Union rules.</p>
<p>&quot;The state would not take any action which did not follow Community rules to the letter, but this doesn't mean that we are not interested in ensuring that a national company can keep going,&quot; he told reporters on the fringes of the Franco-Italian summit here.</p>
<p>Bersani said he would be meeting Olivetti CEO Roberto Colaninno next week.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
